Description: update the cursor position when a key is pressed
 In gtk3 IM module, the key snooper callback only updated the cursor
 location to the IM framework when the IM engine did NOT handle the
 key event. When the IM engine (e.g. Sogou Pinyin) called
 keyEvent.filterAndAccept(), the cursor location was not refreshed, so
 after dragging the application window the candidate window appeared at
 the previous position until the next un-handled key.
 .
 Mirroring fcitx5-qt's behavior (which always updates the IM cursor
 location on every key press regardless of whether the engine handled
 the key), call set_cursor_location_internal() via an idle callback at
 the start of _key_snooper_cb so the candidate window tracks the real
 cursor position.
 .
 Upstream PR: https://github.com/fcitx/fcitx5-gtk/pull/38 (merged)
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: hantengc <1341910529@qq.com>
Origin: https://github.com/fcitx/fcitx5-gtk/pull/38

diff --git a/gtk3/fcitximcontext.cpp b/gtk3/fcitximcontext.cpp
index 47a48a8..d665180 100644
--- a/gtk3/fcitximcontext.cpp
+++ b/gtk3/fcitximcontext.cpp
@@ -1624,6 +1624,12 @@ static gint _key_snooper_cb(GtkWidget *, GdkEventKey *event, gpointer) {
             break;
         }
 
+        /* set_cursor_location_internal() will get origin from X server,
+         * it blocks UI. So delay it to idle callback. */
+        gdk_threads_add_idle_full(
+            G_PRIORITY_DEFAULT_IDLE, (GSourceFunc)_set_cursor_location_internal,
+            g_object_ref(fcitxcontext), (GDestroyNotify)g_object_unref);
+
         _request_surrounding_text(&fcitxcontext);
         if (G_UNLIKELY(!fcitxcontext))
             return FALSE;
